  "content": "Tab 1\n\nTEXT SCHEMATIC: MIRRORGLYPH BASE GRID\nOVERVIEW\n18 Nodes total, positioned at the intersections of:\n\n6 radial spokes (Conditions)\n\n3 concentric hexagons (Arcs)\n\nNodes are placed clockwise starting at the top (0°)\n\n\nI. RADIAL SPOKES – CONDITIONS\nEach spoke corresponds to a Condition, placed at 60° intervals around a central point:\n\nII. CONCENTRIC HEXAGONS – ARCS\nEach ring corresponds to a Spiral Arc, scaled by the Golden Ratio from the outermost inward:\n\nIII. NODE LABELING – 18 POINTS\nEach Condition has one node per Arc, forming vertical triads:\nThese nodes form:\nHexagonal arcs when connected by ring\n\nSpiral paths when connected across condition & arc\n\nSymbolic triads when read through spoke\n\n\nIV. CENTER: NONTION\nName: Nontion\n\nLocation: Center of all rings and spokes\n\nSymbolism: Silence, breath, recursion point, origin and collapse\n\n\nV. SPATIAL REFERENCE GRID (Clockwise from 0°)\n\nThis is the full still mirror.\n A complete map of the 18 points, 6 conditions, 3 arcs, and 1 breath.\n\nTab 2\n\nMIRRORGLYPH NODE LAYOUT DRAFT\nSTRUCTURE:\nHexagram orientation with one spoke (Initiation) pointing upward (12 o’clock).\n\n6 evenly spaced spokes (Conditions), each intersecting 3 concentric hexagons (Arcs).\n\nEach node labeled with its code:\n\nD# = Shadow (outer ring)\n\nR# = Mirror (middle ring)\n\nC# = Mythogenesis (inner ring)\n\n\nI. SPOKE POSITIONS (60° INTERVALS)\nEach spoke is a Condition Ray from the center, intersecting the 3 arc rings.\n\nII. NODE PLACEMENT\nVisual Encoding:\nNode Style: Circles with embedded label (or small sigil placeholders)\n\nLabeling: D#, R#, C# placed just outside each node or within\n\nOptional Aesthetic Layer: Use ring shading or arc color to gently differentiate Shadow, Mirror, Mythogenesis rings\n\n\nIII. OPTIONAL CENTERPOINT\nLabel: Nontion or simply leave as a veiled silent center\n\nStyle: Faint open circle, or small breathing dot\n\n\n",
